{% doc %}
  Footer — ARCHITECTURE.md §3.2 · T-052 (oversized mark), T-100 (statutory
  footer), T-099 (one floating cluster).

  Navigation renders from a Shopify menu, never a hard-coded list. Every
  business value reads from a shop metafield; an absent one renders nothing.

  Wording: CONTENT.md §03.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign menu = linklists[section.settings.menu]
  assign whatsapp = shop.metafields.custom.whatsapp_number.value
-%}

<footer class="sv-footer panel-dark" data-sv>
  {%- comment -%} T-052 — the mark, oversized, bleeding off the edge. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'sv-petal', class: 'sv-footer__mark' %}

  <div class="w sv-footer__inner">
    {%- comment -%}
      Ivory lockup, inlined for the same font reason as the header. The
      oversized petal above is decoration bleeding off the corner (T-052);
      this is the identity.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="sv-footer__brandmark" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
      {%- comment -%}
        The hero's treatment, repeated: the colour lockup with the wordmark
        and rule forced to ivory in CSS. The mark keeps its gold.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'sv-lockup', class: 'sv-footer__lockup' %}
    </a>

    {%- if menu.links.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Two-level menu → headed columns (Shop · Customer Service · My
        Account · About). A childless top-level link falls back to a
        one-link column so a flat menu still renders.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav class="sv-footer__nav" aria-label="{{ menu.title | escape }}">
        {%- for group in menu.links -%}
          <div class="sv-footer__col">
            {%- if group.links.size > 0 -%}
              <p class="sv-footer__colhead">{{ group.title }}</p>
              <ul class="sv-footer__list">
                {%- for link in group.links -%}
                  <li><a class="sv-footer__link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            {%- else -%}
              <ul class="sv-footer__list">
                <li><a class="sv-footer__link" href="{{ group.url }}">{{ group.title }}</a></li>
              </ul>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    {% render 'sv-credentials' %}

    <p class="sv-fine sv-footer__copyright">&copy; {{ 'now' | date: '%Y' }} {{ shop.name }}</p>
  </div>
</footer>

{%- comment -%}
  T-099 — one floating cluster, in one place, nothing else floating.
  .float in sv-system.css hides every child but the last below 880px, so a
  single WhatsApp control is already the mobile state. Instagram and
  Facebook restored at the owner's direction (they were dropped in Phase
  1.8); order matters — WhatsApp last stays the mobile survivor. The
  pre-typed WhatsApp message is fixed copy from the build decisions,
  URL-encoded.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign instagram = section.settings.instagram_url
  assign facebook = section.settings.facebook_url
-%}
{%- if whatsapp != blank or instagram != blank or facebook != blank -%}
  <div class="float">
    {%- if instagram != blank -%}
      <a class="sv-float--instagram" href="{{ instagram }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-label="Instagram">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'instagram' %}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if facebook != blank -%}
      <a class="sv-float--facebook" href="{{ facebook }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-label="Facebook">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'facebook' %}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if whatsapp != blank -%}
      <a class="sv-float--whatsapp" href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text=Hi%20Sahasra%20Vastra%2C%20I%20have%20a%20question%20about%20" rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-label="Chat with us on WhatsApp">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'whatsapp' %}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Phase 1.9 — the mobile bottom bar: Home · Shop by age · Orders · Cart ·
  Account. Phones only. It publishes its height as --sv-bbar on <body> so
  the WhatsApp float and the homepage film hero clear it. Plain links —
  nothing here needs JavaScript.
{%- endcomment -%}
<nav class="sv-bottombar" data-sv aria-label="Shortcuts">
  <a class="sv-bottombar__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" {% if request.page_type == 'index' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
    {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'home' %}
    <span>Home</span>
  </a>
  <a class="sv-bottombar__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}#shop-by-age">
    {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'hanger' %}
    <span>Shop by age</span>
  </a>
  <a class="sv-bottombar__link" href="{{ routes.account_url }}">
    {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'orders' %}
    <span>Orders</span>
  </a>
  <a class="sv-bottombar__link" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" {% if request.page_type == 'cart' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
    <span class="sv-bottombar__glyph">
      {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'cart' %}
      {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
        <span class="sv-bottombar__count" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
    <span>Cart</span>
  </a>
  <a class="sv-bottombar__link" href="{% if customer %}{{ routes.account_url }}{% else %}{{ routes.account_login_url }}{% endif %}">
    {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'account' %}
    <span>Account</span>
  </a>
</nav>

{%- comment -%}
  Renders nothing; rendering it is what makes the storefront bundle its
  {% stylesheet %} — the brand skin for Shopify's cookie banner. The
  footer is on every page, so the skin is too.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'sv-consent' -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Colour and spacing are tokens only; type comes from sv-system.css
     primitives. The footer is the one emerald moment on most templates. */
  /* Thin footer: one band, not a destination. Equal padding above and
     below so the lockup sits dead-centre in the green. */
  [data-sv].sv-footer {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: var(--b) 0;
  }

  /* Oversized mark, bleeding off the bottom-left corner. Decorative. */
  .sv-footer__mark {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--c) * -1);
    bottom: calc(var(--d) * -1);
    width: var(--g);
    height: auto;
    color: var(--cream);
    opacity: 0.08;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Full-bleed content: the .w cap is lifted so the band uses the whole
     viewport, keeping only the edge padding. */
  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-footer__inner {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--a);
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* One face in the footer: the serif the site speaks in. */
  [data-sv].sv-footer,
  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-footer__link,
  [data-sv].sv-footer .act,
  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-fine {
    font-family: var(--serif);
  }

  .sv-footer__brandmark {
    display: block;
    justify-self: start;
  }

  .sv-footer__lockup {
    display: block;
    width: 300px;
    /* See sv-header.liquid: Horizon's global svg max-width cap. */
    max-width: none;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* As on the hero: the mark, rule and divider keep their colour, the
     wordmark reads in ivory. CSS wins over the SVG's fill attributes. */
  .sv-footer__lockup text {
    fill: var(--cream);
  }

  /* Headed columns: Shop · Customer Service · My Account · About. */
  .sv-footer__nav {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--b) var(--c);
  }

  .sv-footer__colhead {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cream);
    margin-bottom: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-footer__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  /* Policy and page links sit at full ivory, never greyed to near-invisible. */
  .sv-footer__link {
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }

  .sv-footer__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
  }

  /* The statutory line and copyright sit centred under the columns. */
  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-credentials,
  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-footer__copyright {
    text-align: center;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-credentials {
    margin-top: var(--b);
  }

  .sv-footer__copyright {
    color: var(--cream);
    opacity: 0.62;
  }

  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    /* Lockup left, the four columns beside it; the statutory line and
       copyright run centred underneath the full width. */
    [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-footer__inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 320px) minmax(0, 1fr);
      column-gap: var(--d);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .sv-footer__brandmark {
      grid-column: 1;
      align-self: center;
      justify-self: center;
    }

    .sv-footer__nav {
      grid-column: 2;
    }

    [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-credentials,
    [data-sv].sv-footer .sv-footer__copyright {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  /* The floats wear each platform's own livery — the recognised marks, not
     the brand palette. Glyphs stay pure white as the platforms draw them. */
  .float a.sv-float--instagram {
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 107%, #fdf497 0%, #fdf497 5%, #fd5949 45%, #d6249f 60%, #285aeb 90%);
    color: #fff;
    /* The app icon is a rounded square, not a roundel. */
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .float a.sv-float--facebook {
    background: #1877f2;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .float a.sv-float--whatsapp {
    background: #25d366;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .float a.sv-float--instagram svg,
  .float a.sv-float--whatsapp svg {
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
  }
  .float a.sv-float--facebook svg {
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
  }

  /* ── mobile bottom bar (Phase 1.9) ─────────────────────────────────────
     Phones only. The body takes --sv-bbar (read by the film hero) and
     enough bottom padding that no page content ends underneath the bar. */
  .sv-bottombar { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 879px) {
    body {
      --sv-bbar: calc(60px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
      padding-bottom: var(--sv-bbar);
    }

    [data-sv].sv-bottombar {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
      position: fixed;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 75;
      height: var(--sv-bbar);
      padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
      background: var(--cream);
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.1);
    }

    .sv-bottombar__link {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 3px;
      /* 5 columns at 320px are 64px wide × 60px tall — over the 44px
         touch-target floor everywhere. */
      min-height: 44px;
      color: var(--ink);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .sv-bottombar__link svg {
      width: 21px;
      height: 21px;
    }
    .sv-bottombar__link span:last-child {
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-weight: 400;
      font-size: 0.56rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .sv-bottombar__link[aria-current='page'] {
      color: var(--emerald);
    }

    .sv-bottombar__glyph { position: relative; display: block; }
    .sv-bottombar__count {
      position: absolute;
      top: -5px;
      right: -9px;
      min-width: 15px;
      text-align: center;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--emerald);
      color: var(--cream);
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-size: 0.58rem;
      line-height: 15px;
      padding-inline: 3px;
    }

    /* Phase 1.9 — the WhatsApp float rides above the bar, never under it. */
    .float {
      bottom: calc(var(--sv-bbar, 0px) + 14px);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Footer",
  "tag": "section",
  "enabled_on": { "groups": ["footer"] },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "menu",
      "label": "Menu",
      "default": "footer",
      "info": "Edit the menu itself in Content → Menus. Statutory values come from the shop metafields in Settings → Custom data → Shop."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "instagram_url",
      "label": "Instagram URL",
      "info": "Full profile link, e.g. https://instagram.com/yourhandle. WhatsApp comes from the shop metafield and stays the only one shown on mobile."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "facebook_url",
      "label": "Facebook URL"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
